'''Ghurz of the Grand Icon''' is a [[Khorne]] [[Dark Apostle]], in the [[Iron Butchers (Warband)|Iron Butchers]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]], which is part of the larger [[Gore-forged]] Warband.{{Fn|1}}
==History==
However everyone in the [[Chaos Warband|Warbands]] know the Iron Butchers are the [[Daemon Prince]] [[Vorghor]]'s followers first and foremost. The only way a [[Gore-forged]] leader maintains his position is by dominating his followers, but should a new champion join the Warband, then a power struggle is all but guaranteed to break out. Such was the case when Vorghor joined and it is only a matter of time until the Daemon Prince attempts to physically wrest control of the Gore-forged from its current leader, [[Ar'ghurak]].{{Fn|1}}

In the battlefield, the [[Dark Apostle]] heralds the coming of [[Vorghor]] himself and Ghurz also carries the [[Daemon Prince]]'s [[Chaos Icon]] as well. He has [[Dark Disciples]] that serve him and two sword wielding [[Chaos Cultists]], known as '''Blood-monks''', accompany Ghurz into battle. They are untested aspirants, who seek to prove themselves worthy of the [[Temple Blade]]s, that have been loaned to them. Should both Blood-monks survive the battle they accompanied Ghurz into, then they are sworn to duel each other to the death.{{Fn|1}} 
==Trivia==
The [[Gore-forged]] and the [[Iron Butchers (Warband)|Iron Butchers]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[James Ashbey]], for the [[White Dwarf]] magazine's 2023 '''A Tale of Four Warlords''' competition.{{Fn|1}} 

