Gideon (Ultramarines).wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Gideon''' is a grizzled [[Assault Intercessor]] [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] in the [[Ultramarines 2nd Company]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
In [[M42]], his squadron was part of the strike force, led by [[Space Marine Lieutenant|Lieutenant]] [[Vincius]], that was sent to destroy the [[Chaos Lord|Chaos Warlord]] [[Hargaal Xere]], after he established a stronghold on [[Bakhar Prime]]. After they arrived in the [[Eastern Fringes]]' [[Bakhar Sector]], though, Xere's forces began to attack worlds that were close by to Bakhar Prime. The strike force became stretched thin as a result, and later could only spare Gideon's squadron to answer a plea for aid from [[Zanzamon]]. When they arrived at the [[Industrial World]], however, Gideon's squadron discovered it was being attacked by a small [[Necron]] force from the [[Szarekhan Dynasty]].{{Fn|1}}  

They soon learned, though, that [[Zanzamon]] was a [[Necron Tomb World]] and they faced just a vanguard, of the awakening legions beneath the world's surface. Gideon quickly requested aid to deal with this emerging threat, but due to its battles with [[Hargaal Xere]], it would be weeks or months before the strike force's reinforcements arrived. Despite this setback and being heavily outnumbered, Gideon knew that his squadron had a unique opportunity to strike a telling blow for the [[Imperium]]. The [[Intercessors]] then fought to eliminate the awakened vanguard and discover a way into the [[Szarekhan Dynasty]]'s tomb complex. If they succeeded, Gideon and his squadron could be able to destroy great swathes of the Dynasty's army, before the Necrons could rise up and claim Zanzamon.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [https://web.archive.org/web/20210903213125/https://warhammer40000.com/fireteam/?utm_source=WarhammerCommunity&utm_medium=Post&utm_campaign=BringtheWar-torn41stMillenniumtoYourKitchenTableWithTheseUpcomingBoardGames02092021&utm_content=BringtheWar-torn41stMillenniumtoYourKitchenTableWithTheseUpcomingBoardGames02092021 Warhammer 40,000: Fireteam website (archived)] PDF Rule Book, pgs. 12-13 (Last accessed on 2 September 2021)

