Glorian Sarck.wikitext:
{{OrdoMalleusPortal}}{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Glorian Sarck''' was a former [[Radical]] [[Ordo Malleus]] [[Inquisitor]], who was tutored by the [[Xanthism]] founder [[Zaranchek Xanthus]].{{Fn|1}}  
==History==
When [[Zaranchek Xanthus|Xanthus]] was condemned and executed for [[Heresy]], Sarck and and his former student [[Mynarc]] fled from the [[Ordo Malleus]]. The two [[Inquisitor]]s would later find themselves on [[Cneiras]] and discovered a nocturnal race of troglodytes there, who openly worshiped [[Chaos]]. Their continued associations with the creatures led to Sarck becoming corrupted and embracing Heresy. However once Mynarc learned of this, he attacked Sarck while his former master was conducting a depraved ritual. Sarck's life would be ended by his own blade and the ritual was disrupted as a result. This caused the Inquisitor's soul to be drawn into his blade, where the trapped Sarck began uttering dark whispers to his former student. Mynarc kept the sword afterwards and then fled from the troglodytes, but this and constantly hearing Sarck's voice, began to change the Inquisitor. He eventually gave in to his former master's corrupting influence and embraced Chaos as well. The Inquisitor then began to be guided by Sarck's soul and when he was found to be a Heretic, Mynarc was declared [[Excommunicate Traitoris]].{{Fn|1}}

