Glutt.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
{{otheruses|USE=[[Sanctioned Psyker]]|OTHERUSE=[[Genestealer Patriarch]]|OTHERPAGE=Foresire Glutt}}
'''Glutt''' was a [[Sanctioned Psyker]] of the [[Imperial Guard]] who fought during the [[Chaos]] insurrection of [[Sepus Prime]].{{Fn|1}}


==History==
Glutt was brutally trained for years by the [[Scholastia Psykana]].{{Fn|1}}

He was assigned to the [[Imperial Guard]] and fought during the [[Chaos]] insurrection of [[Sepus Prime]]. The savagery of the war wiped away all the aphorisms taught to him by the Scholastia Psykana, except the phrase "Through the needle's eye, I live or die", which he used as a mantra to keep himself focused. The rest of his detail was wiped out before reaching [[Tadmor Ridge]] on their way to the front lines. Glutt started to make his way back to the barracks.{{Fn|1}}

After two days, near the barracks, Glutt came across Lieutenant [[Sorov]]'s unit, who were preparing to shoot down [[Planetary Governor|Governor]] [[Narbo]]'s [[Aquila Lander]]. They were successful, but the Governor emerged from the wreck, and transformed into a [[Chaos Spawn]], killing all except Glutt, Sorov, and [[Vox-officer]] [[Federak]]. Glutt unleashed his abilities, and destroyed the Spawn before it could kill Sorov and Federak.{{Fn|1}}

Despite Narbo being killed, Commander [[Ortegal]] redesignated Sepus Prime as Contaminated, and ordered that the entire planet be [[Virus Bomb]]ed, along with everyone on it, leaving the Imperial Guard regiments to die there. When this happened, Glutt managed to survive by using his psychic abilites to become one with the explosions.{{Fn|1}}

==Description==
Glutt had a slight build.{{Fn|1}}

==Equipment==
During his time as an Imperial Sanctioned Psyker, Glutt wielded [[Force Staff|an eagle-headed staff]], and a [[Laspistol]] with a scope. He wore a heavy black coat and peaked cap, and had a [[rebreather]].{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
===Notes===
*Lieutenant [[Sorov]] said to his unit "you might even get off this rancid planet", implying that their regiment was not from [[Sepus Prime]].{{Fn|1}}

