Gorley.wikitext:
{{TanithPortal}}
'''Gorley''' was a [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]] of the [[Tanith First and Only]], commanding the [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment's]] [[Imperial Guard Platoon|fifth platoon]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
Gorley and Five Platoon were present on [[Oskray Island]] when the forces of the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]] invaded the planet [[Sapiencia]]. He and Sergeant [[Ceglan Varl|Varl's]] platoons were some of the first infantry to hit the beaches of Oskray when the [[Imperial]] assault faltered, as a number of the [[Basilisk]]s that were going to be used to breach the sea walls on the island were dropped in the [[Bay of Belano]] short of their target and were rendered inoperable by the seawater.{{Fn|1}}

Eventually one of the Imperial [[troop-ship]]s crashed through the wall after being shot down by [[Chaos|enemy]] fire. This created an opening, but it still wasn't wide enough to bring heavy armour through and the [[Kith|island's defenders]] quickly had the breach covered. Nonetheless it allowed the remaining Basilisks to form up on the beach and attempt to widen the gap. [[Trooper]] [[Domor]], however, spotted a passage running through the upper wall that had been split open. Trooper [[Dermon Caffran|Caffran]] suggested that a fire-team of Tanith could scale the wall and get inside the tunnel, using it to infiltrate [[Oskray Island One|the island's hive complex]]. Gorley volunteered to lead the fire-team while Varl (who was unable to make the climb) brought injured troopers back down the beach to safety. A number of troopers successfully made it inside the wall but unfortunately Gorley, who had waited until last to make the climb, was too slow and ended up being caught in the friendly artillery barrage trying to widen the gap in the wall and was blown to smithereens.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
