Gorok.wikitext:
{{TauPortal}}
'''Gorok''' of [[Clan T'cha]] was a [[Kroot]] [[Shaper]] present on [[Gravalax]] during the [[Gravalax Incident]] in late [[M41]].

==History==
{{spoiler|source=For the Emperor (Novel)}}
Shortly after [[Commissar]] [[Ciaphas Cain]]'s arrival on Gravalax with the [[Valhallan 597th]], he and his friend [[Toren Divas]] were attacked by a mob of pro-[[Tau]] humans, before Gorox appeared and called them off.  He struck up an acquaintance with Cain, which proved useful later.{{Fn|1a}}

When war threatened to break out between the Tau and Imperial forces on the planet, both made the independent decision to send a scouting party into the tunnels under the capital city, to locate the third party stirring up trouble.  Cain's party, led by [[Inquisitor]] [[Amberley Vail]], bumped into the [[Tau]] expedition, which included Gorok.  Their previous acquaintance helped to broker a temporary truce with the Imperials (though not, unfortunately, before one of the Kroot was killed by an Imperial sniper; Gorok appeared to take this phlegmatically, complimenting the [[Valhallan]] sniper on his skill).  Because of the [[Kroot]]'s ability to "taste" genetic variation, Gorok's observations alerted Vail and Cain to the true nature of their opponents - a [[Genestealer cult]].{{Fn|1b}}

When it became apparent to Gorok that the [[Genestealer Hybrid]]s had discovered the head of the slain Kroot, he acted to destroy the remains rather than let the Kroot's genetics fall into the Genestealers' hands.  However, as soon as he opened fire, the party was discovered.  As they retreated, Cain last saw Gorok being torn apart by a Purestrain Genestealer.{{Fn|1c}}

==Sources==
