Graevus.wikitext:
{{SoulDrinkersPortal}}
'''Graevus''' was a [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] of the [[Soul Drinkers]] [[Chapter]], commanding the [[Assault Squad]] designated [[Squad Graevus]].{{Fn|1a}}

Graevus was part of the Soul Drinkers strike force led by [[Space Marine Commander|Commander]] [[Caeon]] that took part in an [[Administratum]]-organised raid of the [[Van Skorvold Star Fort]].  When the Soul Drinkers [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] allies, led by [[Magos|Archmagos]] [[Khobotov]], stole a [[Soulspear|relic of the Chapter]] from the station's vaults and threatened to destroy the star fort if the [[Space Marines]] did not back down, Graevus and his squadron were among the Soul Drinkers led by [[Librarian]] [[Sarpedon]] that assaulted Khobotov's [[Geryon Ordinatus]] platform to try to reclaim the relic.{{Fn|1a}}

Following this incident, the Soul Drinkers were declared [[Excommunicate Traitoris]].  Rejecting the [[Imperium]] (though not the [[Emperor of Mankind|Emperor]] himself), Sarpedon led the bulk of the Chapter in going [[Renegade Chapter|renegade]] and Graevus was among them.  In the process of doing so, several Soul Drinkers were "blessed" with [[Mutant|enhancements]] by a being known as [[Abraxes|The Architect of Fate]].  Graevus was one of these, his right hand becoming warped and elongated, to the point he could wield his [[power axe]] one-handed.{{Fn|1b}}

