Gregor Ormond.wikitext:
{{ImperialKnightsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[sacristan]] who served [[House Cadmus]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Gregory Ormund is a sacristan who trained on the [[Forge World]] [[Raisa]]. After many long years of study among the [[Gryphonne IV|Gryphonnen]] [[magi]], he became an honoured [[artificer]]. His great knowledge and expertise was used to maintain the [[Knight|steeds]] of House Cadmus.{{Fn|1}}

Gregor Ormond was another survivor of the Gryphonnen disaster whose manner of escape had left him stranded amid the Mechanicus refugees. He had become separated from the rest of the House Cadmus entourage when a storm of [[tyranid]] [[Mycetic Spore|spores]] descended upon their [[drop-keep]], birthing a horde of brood-creatures into their midst. The old man had escaped the massacre that followed, and through sheer good fortune managed to board a [[Slovo VI|Slovo VI orbital conveyor]] and blast free from the nightmare alongside a dozen maniples of [[skitarii]].{{Fn|1}}

In the slow process of organisation that followed the exodus from Gryphonne IV he and Sir [[Edgar Lorristan]] had been brought together aboard the ''[[Peregrinus]]'' along with ''[[Vortigern (Knight Armiger)|Vortigern]]'', each a stranger to the others. Ormond was at least twice Edgar's age; a short grey moustache and thinning hair completed a face that had seen more than its share of years. He was a grim, downtrodden sort of man, much given to bemoaning his state and station.{{Fn|1}}

