Grenfeld.wikitext:
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''The whole principle of naval fighting is to be free to go anywhere with every damned thing the Navy possesses.'''''<br>
''Captain Grenfeld''{{Fn|1a}}
|}}
Captain '''Grenfeld''' was a captain of the [[Imperial Navy]] during the [[Gothic War]], where he commanded the ''[[Hammer of Justice]]'' well, leading to a renewed interest in [[Nova Cannon]]s across [[Segmentum Obscuras]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|2}}

== History ==
Grenfeld attained the rank of captain and command of the [[Dominator Class Cruiser]] ''[[Hammer of Justice]]'' under the command of [[Lord Admiral]] [[Cornelius von Ravensburg]] of [[Battlefleet Gothic]] at some point prior to the outbreak of the [[Gothic War]] in 143.[[M41]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}} The ''Hammer of Justice'' was the only Dominator Class vessel in Battlefleet Gothic, and one of the few in [[Segmentum Obscurus]], where it was relatively rare, and built to act as a support for major fleet actions and planetary assaults.{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|2}} The ship had an undistinguished record, and performed poorly on exercises during this time.{{Fn|1b}}

However, when the war commenced, Grenfeld commanded the ''Hammer'' admirably, rising to the challenge, and demonstrating able use of the ship's powerful but unwieldy [[Nova Cannon]].{{Fn|1b}} He used it during the [[Port Maw Blockade]] to destroy the [[Chaos]] [[Devastation Class Cruiser]] ''[[Unforgivable]]'', and again at the [[Raid on Alios]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|3}}

His command and expert use of this rare ship class led many other vessels in Battlefleet Gothic to undertake major refits, replacing their prow weapons with [[Nova Cannon]]s throughout the war.{{Fn|1b}} After the war, this led to a reassessment of [[Dominator Class Cruiser]]s across [[Segmentum Obscurus]], with many other battlefleets showing an interest in what had previously been a class of ship normally used in [[Ultima Segmentum]].{{Fn|2}}

