Gulthorg.wikitext:
{{NurglePortal}}
'''Gulthorg the Blighted''' is a [[Death Guard]]-affiliated{{Fn|2}} [[Chaos Lord]], who commands the [[Chaos Space Marine|corrupted]] [[Space Marine Chapter]] known as the [[Sons of Rot]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
In [[M42]], he became a commander of one of [[Abaddon the Despoiler]]'s [[Ark of Omen]]s, after Gulthorg pledged to use it to track down one of a series of artefacts known as a [[Key-Fragment]]. Each Fragment had a unique [[warp]] signature and Gulthorg's Ark, [[Ogre]], tracked its location to a fort on the [[Fortress World]] [[Cortosa III]]. However while he had pledged to focus on recovering the Fragment and then return it to Abaddon, Gulthorg decided to corrupt Cortosa III instead. The [[Chaos Lord]] intended for the Fortress World to serve as his seat of power, to build a suppurating empire in Nurgle's name and would only return with the Key-Fragment once Cortosa III was his. With that, Gulthorg unleashed the might of the Ogre against the world, along with the various forces that composed his [[Balefleet]].{{Fn|1}}

These included Gulthorg's [[Sons of Rot]] [[Chapter]], along with the [[Morbidax]] [[Traitor Guard]] [[Regiment]]s, the [[Chaos Knights]] of [[House Gnaw]], the [[Dark Mechanicum]] [[Vivisector Squadron]]s of Archmagos [[Ovloch]] and the long-time rivals of the [[Plaguecrows]] and [[Vermin Guard]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]s. The Warbands' [[Chaos Champion|Champion]]s were sworn enemies as well and had only offered their allegiance to Gulthorg so that the other could not gain the Chaos Lord's sole favor. With this might at his command, Gulthorg's forces began invading Cortosa III, before the [[Adepta Sororitas]] and [[Black Templars]] stationed within the [[Cortosa System]] could reach the besieged world. He would also unleash viral weapons upon the Fortress World, which reduced those struck by them into slime, that [[Daemon]]s serving [[Abaddon]]'s ally [[Vashtorr]] crawled out of. Even with all these forces at his command, though, the Imperials defending Cortosa III fought back fiercely against the invaders.{{Fn|1}} 

After days of fighting, their attacks forced Gulthorg and the [[Sons of Rot]] to return to the [[Ogre]], in order to defend it from the [[Imperials]]. Unbeknownst to the [[Chaos Lord]], however, Abaddon had planted [[Alpha Legion]] members within the [[Balefleets]] to circumvent any [[Ark of Omen|Ark]] commanders that refused to follow his orders. When Gulthorg reentered the Ogre, its Alpha Legion acted at once to claim Cortosa III's Key-Fragment for Abaddon. Using hijacked [[Vox]] channels, they issued orders to a large portion of the Chaos Lord's forces, to attack the fort that held the Fragment. It was successful and Alpha Legion escaped with the Key-Fragment, while the Imperials advanced to capitalize on Gulthorg's ground forces now being horribly out of position.{{Fn|1}}

