Gunnlaugur.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''Gunnlaugur''', known as '''Skullhewer''', was a [[Space Marine Sergeant|pack leader]] of the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]]. He was the leader of [[Járnhamar Pack]], in the [[Blackmanes]] [[Great Company]].{{Fn|1b}}

==Biography==
As a mortal, Gunnlaugur was the chieftain of a [[Fenris]]ian tribe known as the [[Gaellings]].{{Fn|1b}}

Gunnlaugur served in Járnhamar Pack under the Wolf Guard [[Hjortur Ageir Hvat Bloodfang|Hjortur Bloodfang]].{{Fn|1c}} When Hjortur died, he had not named a successor but it was known that he had two in mind: Gunnlaugur and [[Ingvar Orm Eversson|Gyrfalkon]].{{Fn|1a}} Ordinarily, the two would have competed to determine which would ascend to the rank of Wolf Guard and become the new pack-leader. However, the Great Company's [[Wolf Lord]] at the time, [[Berek Thunderfist]], chose around that time to second Gyrfalkon to the [[Deathwatch]]. As a result, Gunnlaugur's promotion was uncontested.{{Fn|1b}}

Shortly into {{PAGENAME}}'s tenure as Pack Leader, his former rival [[Ingvar]] returned from the [[Deathwatch]].{{Fn|1b}} The two had a tense relationship at first, but after many arguments and confrontations learned to work together during the battle on [[Ras Shakeh]].{{Fn|1c}} After the battle, Gunnlaugur learns to trust Ingvar's advice and stops attempting to sideline him.{{Fn|1e}}

During the subsequent battle with the [[Sorcerer]] [[Mycelite]] aboard the [[Space Hulk]] ''[[Festerax]]'', {{PAGENAME}} led the assault alongside [[Njal Stormcaller]].{{Fn|3a}} Afterwards, he worked with Ingvar and the rest of Járnhamar Pack in rescuing [[Baldr]] from execution after he was condemned as a [[Psyker|Witch]], becoming fugitives from their own Chapter in the process.{{Fn|3b}}

{{PAGENAME}} continued to lead the Pack during its time as renegades aboard the ''[[Amethyst Suzeraine]]'', seeking the "Fulcrum" as a chance of redemption.{{Fn|4a}} They were eventually able to track the trail of Fulcrum to [[Ojada VII]], revealing it to be the traitorous [[Cardinal]] [[Leon Chirastes]].{{Fn|4b}} This led them to [[Cadia]] to rescue their [[Wolf Lord]] [[Ragnar Blackmane]] from Chirastes' agents, but during the search {{PAGENAME}} stayed behind to help a group of [[Cadian Shock Troopers]] amid the [[13th Black Crusade]]. In the subsequent fight against [[Chaos Space Marine]]s, [[Jorundur]] was killed while Gunnlaugur was severely wounded.{{Fn|4c}} However, he was able to be evacuated into orbit and given medical treatment, reuniting with Ingvar and the surviving members of his pack aboard Ragnar's [[Frigate]] ''[[Dawnrunner]]''.{{Fn|4d}}

==Wargear==
Gunnlaugur's favoured weapon was a [[thunder hammer]] that shared his epithet, named ''[[skulbrotsjorór]]''.{{Fn|1c}}

==Notes==
*{{Endn|Note 1}}: In [https://www.blacklibrary.com/warhammer-40000/novels/blood-of-asaheim-ebook.html Black Library's webpage for Blood of Asaheim], Gunnlaugur's name is spelled '''Gunnlaugr'''.{{Fn|2}} In the novel itself, however, it is consistently spelled '''Gunnlaugur'''.{{Fn|1a}} 

