Gylon.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
'''First Zealot Gylon''' was a [[Demagogue]] of a [[Chaos Cult]] on [[Nekkaris]] in late [[M41]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
His awakening began on what he called the '''Day of Truth''', when the [[Chaos Lord]] [[Da'ka Jumoke]], who had secretly invaded [[Nekkaris]], corrupted Gylon into the ways of [[Chaos]]. He would then become a [[Demagogue]] and created a [[Chaos Cult]], which later began an uprising with Jumoke's [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]. The world's capital was then seized by the Cult, who began killing anyone not willing to worship the Chaos Gods. The [[Flesh Tearers]] would then come to aid Nekkaris and began advancing upon the capital with the world's military. However before the [[Imperial]]s could reach the capital, the Cult and Warband launched a continuous artillery barrage from armored vehicles, which stopped the advance cold. Even with the Flesh Tearers' might, they would not be able to survive the Chaos forces' rate of fire and so [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Temel]] was selected to lead a group of [[Scout]]s to destroy the artillery in a set time limit. Doing so, would then allow the Imperials to reach the capital and end the rebellion. While the Scouts would succeed, the Flesh Tearers would instead leave Nekkaris in favor of answering a [[Cryptus Campaign|plea for aid]] from the [[Blood Angels]].{{Fn|1}} 

The [[Flesh Tearers]]' [[Chapter Master]], [[Gabriel Seth]], felt time was of the essence, so he refused to wait to evacuate [[Temel]]'s [[Scout]]s and instead regretfully left them to their fates. Gylon soon informed [[Da'ka Jumoke|Jumoke]] of this and hoped that the [[Chaos Lord]], would give the order to fully seize the capital from the [[Imperium]]'s control. To the [[Demagogue]]'s dismay, however, Jumoke instead gave the order for his [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] to begin leaving [[Nekkaris]]. When Gylon pleaded with the Chaos Lord not to abandon his [[Chaos Cult|Cult]], an enraged Jumoke grabbed the Demagogue by the face and lifted him up. The Chaos Lord then explained, as be began crushing Gylon's skull, that he did not care about Nekkaris or the Demagogue's Cult. Jumoke's only purpose for invading the world, was to fulfill his patron's desire to see the Flesh Tearers' fall to [[Heresy]]. Thus Chaos Lord's efforts on Nekkaris were not fruitless, as he knew the decision to leave the [[Chapter]]'s Scouts behind, had scarred Seth's soul. With enough such scars, the Chapter Master would fall and with him so would the Flesh Tearers. However since the Chapter was now gone, this meant Nekkaris was no longer useful to aid Jumoke in his goal. The same applied to Gylon as well and the Chaos Lord then ignited the Demogogue aflame with his gauntlet.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[A Son's Burden (Short Story)]]

