Gzrel.wikitext:
{{CSMPortal}}
{{KhornePortal}}
'''Gzrel''' was [[Chaos Lord]] of the [[Khorne]]ate warband known as [[The Harrowing]].

== History ==
Gzrel's preferred tactics included the use of [[mutant]]s; all of the [[Chaos Space Marines]] in his warband were changed by minor warp mutations, a lesser version of [[Possessed]] Marines.{{Fn|1x}} Gzrel also used [[Chaos Spawn|slave beasts]] as trackers and attack dogs.{{Fn|1x}}

Despite [[Khorne]]'s traditional hatred of sorcery, Gzrel used several [[Chaos Sorcerers]] in his warband, keeping four as his inner circle: [[Xiatsis]], [[Cottadaron]], [[Horkos]] and [[Maroth]], the last of whom was Gzrel's High Magister and second-in-command of The Harrowing.{{Fn|1x}}

After a recent victory over a [[Renegade Space Marine]] [[chapter]] and the take-over of their ship, the ''[[Titan Child]]'', Gzrel and the Harrowing were approached by an emissary from a renegade [[Thousand Sons]] warband. The emissary, [[Tolbek]], quickly realized that "Horkos" was in fact [[Ahzek Ahriman]], his former brother, in disguise. Conversing with Ahriman via [[telepathy]], Tolbek asked Ahriman to come with him. When Ahriman refused, [[Tolbek]] attacked. Ahriman's long-disused [[psychic]] abilities were awoken, and he killed Tolbek, along with killed Gzrel and two of his pet sorcerers, leaving only Maroth alive.{{Fn|1a}}

Ahriman then proceeded to free the survivors of the  renegade [[chapter]] and [[Tech Priest]] [[Carmenta]], who killed the rest of the Harrowing and took back the ''Titan Child'', before fleeing the sector.{{Fn|1b}}

