Hakhroth.wikitext:
{{WordBearersPortal}}
'''Hakhroth''' is a [[Sorcerer]] in [[The Blessed]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] and was a [[Dark Apostle]] of the [[Word Bearers]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], during the [[Horus Heresy]] and [[Great Crusade]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
He was noted as being an early convert to the [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]'s [[Warrior Lodge]]s and was a pupil of the mighty [[Erebus]] as well. When the [[Horus Heresy]] neared its end, Hakhroth served{{Fn|1}} under [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Darokh'Var]] and was aboard his warship, the [[Firebrand (Warship)|Firebrand]], as the [[Word Bearers]] traveled to [[Battle for Terra|invade]] [[Terra]]. However before they reached it, the Firebrand became trapped in the [[Warp]] for several days. When the Firebrand finally re-emerged, though, Darokh'Var and his forces realized that over a thousand years had passed. They soon discovered that the [[Imperium]] had defeated the [[Traitor Legion]]s, who had been forced to flee into the [[Eye of Terror]]. Being that the Captain was fanatically loyal to his [[Primarch]] [[Lorgar]], Darokh'Var then led his forces to attack nearby Imperial worlds, before fleeing back into the Warp. Once again, however, the Firebrand became trapped in the Warp and when it re-emerged yet another thousand years had passed. Darokh'Var would continue his attacks despite this and a total of several decades would pass in the Warp for the Word Bearers, while millennia passed in [[Realspace]]{{Fn|2}}. It was during this time, that Hakhroth gained the ability to commit [[Sorcerer|sorcery]], but this also left him with a wizened appearance. His powers, though, drew the veneration of his Brothers, as it was an obvious mark of the [[Chaos Gods]]' favor. By the time they became [[The Blessed]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]], Hakhroth's influence led him to become Darokh'Var's trusted advisor, whose council was highly valued.{{Fn|1}}

