Haldor Twinfang.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a member of the [[Space Wolves]]' Third [[Great Company]], among the first [[Blood Claws|Blooded Claws]] inducted into the [[Chapter]] after the [[Second Founding]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
===Induction===
'''Ove-Thost''', as he was known before his ascension, was a warrior of [[Fenris]] who nearly succumbed to the [[Wulfen|Curse of the Wulfen]] during his [[Trial of Morkai]]. As he neared the [[the Fang|Aett]], he fought a predator with three rows of fangs, taking two of these to pin together the wound it left on his shoulder. At the gates of the Aett he was met by the [[Wolf Priest]] [[Brannak]], who later threaded the twin fangs on a leather chord for the renamed Haldor, giving him the name '''Haldor Twinfang'''.{{Fn|1a}}

Twinfang was inducted into [[Wolf Lord|Jarl]] [[Aeska Brokenlip]]'s Company, the Third [[Great Company]], one of the first new [[Blood Claws]] since the [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] had been made a [[Chapter]] by the [[Second Founding]]. Brannak continued to take a special interest in Twinfang, giving him a two-headed axe of dark metal and telling him to learn its name. At the feast to celebrate the new Blood Claws, Twinfang left the feasting hall and met the [[Primarch]] [[Leman Russ (Primarch)|Leman Russ]], who saw his axe and told him the saga of [[the Lion and the Wolf]].{{Fn|1a}}

===Early Service===
Twinfang's first battle was against the [[orks]] on the [[agri-world]] of [[Pholeses X]], followed by numerous other encounters with various [[xenos]] in his first campaign tour. Years later, he became a [[Grey Hunter|Hunter]] and master of his pack of six.{{Fn|1b}}

===The Cataclysm of Faith===
The appearance of the [[space hulk]] ''[[Cataclysm of Faith]]'' marked the first signs of the [[Chaos Space Marines|Great Enemy]]'s return, carrying a force of [[Emperor's Children]] among its hordes of twisted, degenerate creatures. After [[Aeska Brokenlip]] died fighting in the space hulk, Twinfang took his pack as part of a fleet from multiple [[Chapter]]s to bring vengeance to the hulk. The campaign against lasted years, drawing in forces from the [[Dark Angels]], [[Ultramarines]], [[White Scars]], and several of their successors. On the eve of the last battle on the desert world of [[Iela]], Twinfang fought an honour duel with the Dark Angel [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Otho (Dark Angels)|Otho]].{{Fn|1b}}

==Wargear==
Twinfang carries the relic axe ''[[Wyrdfast]]''.{{Fn|1b}}

==Sources==
