Hamadrya.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
[[Image:Hamadrya.jpg|thumb|right|200px|The Hamadrya]]
The '''Hamadrya''' is a [[Chaos]]-spawned creature that acts as the [[Familiar (Chaos)|familiar]] to [[Lugft Huron]], the leader of the [[Red Corsairs]].{{Fn|1}}

The creature's exact nature and origin are unclear. It supposedly appeared after the fall of [[Badab]], where Huron was greviously wounded. Many of the Corsairs whispered that, while the [[Apothecaries]] laboured to repair his broken body, his soul wandered free, eventually making a pact with the [[Ruinous Powers]] that would enable him to survive. The Hamadrya appeared at his side then, almost as insubstantial as a wisp of vapour. As Huron recovered and his power grew, the Hamadrya likewise grew and took on a more cohesive shape. Its exact appearance is unknown; sometimes it is invisible, and when it chooses to appear it can be avian, reptilian, or mammalian in shape.{{Fn|2}}

Similarly, the gifts it bestows on Blackheart are uncertain and often changeable. At times it endows him with the [[Warptime]] ability wielded by [[Chaos Sorcerer]]s{{Fn|1}}. At others, it appears to shield him from psychic attack or detection, similar to a [[Null Rod]].{{Fn|2}} Rumours are that it also allows Huron to read others' thoughts, and he has thus evaded assassination a hundred times over.{{Fn|3}}

The Hamadrya's abilities were once limited to the boundaries of the [[Maelstrom]], since it needed [[warp]] energy to sustain itself. This imposed a limitation on Huron's ability to venture abroad, so he consulted his [[Librarian]]s, and eventually succeeded in binding the soul of a powerful Sorcerer in a vessel, which would allow Huron to continue to enjoy "the blessing of the [[Gods of Chaos|Four]]" outside the Maelstrom.{{Fn|2}}

