Hamath Kraatos.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
'''Hamath Kraatos''' is the [[Space Marine Sergeant|Vigilator-Sergeant]] of the [[Minotaurs]] 9<sup>th</sup> [[Devastator]] company, serving as the second-in-command.{{Fn|1}}

[[File:HamathKraatos.jpeg|thumb|right|250px|Hamath Kraatos miniature{{fn|2}}]]

==Biography==
Kraatos' rise through the ranks has been unwarrantedly rapid by the standards of many Chapters. He is phenomenally proficient with ballistic weapons as well as a ruthless and calculating leader - with a murderous temper.{{fn|1}}

Given command of a demi-company, Kraatos distinguished himself in the early stages of the [[Orphean War]] by defending a fuelling station at '''Attedum'''. Here, he used the human workers and servitors as bait to draw out the enemy, [[dark eldar|eldar corsairs]] driven from their lairs by the [[necron]] advance, corralling them in the central refinery before cutting them down in a series of crossfires and enfilades. Three hours later over two hundred [[Kabal|Kabalites]] lay dead, with unexpectedly low civilian casualties of only six in ten.{{fn|1}}

==Equipment==
Kraatos carries a [[Signum]] and a [[Heavy Bolter]]. In addition to standard ammunition, he carries a limited supply of artificer-engineered '''Assassin Bolts''', hypersonic rounds that replace the standard propellant with short-burn magna-fusion charges and the mass-reactive warhead (which would not endure the fusion discharge) with solid slugs. Due to their extreme speed and density, they are both highly destructive and extremely accurate.{{fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Imperial Armour Volume Twelve - The Fall of Orpheus]], pg. 149
