[[File:War-of-the-Fang-cover.jpg|450px|thumb|right|Harek Ironhelm in combat with [[Magnus]] on the slopes of [[The Fang]].]]
'''Harek Eireik Eireiksson'''{{Fn|1c}}, known colloquially as '''Harek Ironhelm''', was [[Great Wolf]] of the [[Space Wolves]] in [[M32]]{{Fn|2}} when the Chapter faced one of its greatest threats, the [[Battle of the Fang|invasion]] of their homeworld of [[Fenris]] by the [[Thousand Sons]], led personally by [[Magnus the Red]].

Obsessed with tracking down and destroying the Thousand Sons due to the [[Burning of Prospero|hatred]] between the two former [[Space Marine Legion|Legions]], Harek was busy pursuing supposed Thousand Sons forces when Magnus' invasion began.{{Fn|1a}} Harek was lured to the world of [[Arvion]], where he battled [[Chaos]] forces allied to the Thousand Sons as part of a grand distraction by Magnus. When he heard of what was befalling his homeworld Fenris, Ironhelm raced to the planet.{{Fn|3}} Ironhelm only arrived at the closing stages of the battle, intervening in the battle between Magnus and [[Bjorn]] and plunging his [[Drop Pod]] onto the [[Daemon Prince]]. Engaging a wounded Magnus in personal combat, Ironhelm was killed by the Primarch.{{Fn|1b}}

After the battle had been won, [[Jarl]] [[Arvek Kjarlskar]] became Great Wolf of the Chapter.{{Fn|1c}}

Harek Ironhelm was interred with great honour in a tomb on the side of the Fang. His tomb became a regular pilgrimage site for the Chapter's [[Rune Priest]]s, who are reminded not only of Ironhelm's valour, but also of the folly in trusting visions granted by [[Chaos]]{{Fn|2}}.

