Harik Morn.wikitext:
{{IronHandsPortal}}
'''Ancient{{Fn|1}} Harik Morn'''{{Fn|2}} was a [[Contemptor Dreadnought]] in the [[Iron Hands]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], who took part in the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[File:Morn.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Harik Morn{{Fn|1}}]]
Prior to being entombed within a [[Contemptor Dreadnought|Dreadnought]], Morn was a [[Terra]]n-born [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] in the [[Avernii Clan]]'s First Order and had a dry sense of humour. During the [[Great Crusade]], he took part in destroying [[Ork]] [[Kill Kroozer]]s under his [[Primarch]] [[Ferrus Manus]]' command in the [[Fist of Iron]]. However, in one such operation near a [[Warp]] anomaly, an Iron Hands [[Strike Cruiser]] unexpectedly appeared among the wreckage. Morn was handpicked by [[Ferrus Manus]] to join him in the boarding party along with Sergeant [[Gabriel Santar]] and [[Mechanicum]] representative Xanthus.{{Fn|2}}

The group discovered clues that the derelict ship came from some point in the future. Unidentified xenoforms began attacking the boarding party, forcing Ferrus to issue a fighting withdrawal. Even while defending himself Morn disagreed with leaving a Legion ship at the hands of the xenos, but his [[Primarch]] remained firm.{{Fn|2}}

Morn was one of [[Clan Avernii]]'s most respected warriors and once served in the Avernii's [[Terminator]] Centuries of Ferrus' [[Space Marine Honour Guard|Honour Guard]].  As part of the Honour Guard, Morn fought beside [[Ferrus Manus|Manus]] throughout countless battles, until he was mortally wounded at the height of the [[Battle of Gardinaal Prime]] when his body was crushed by one of the gargantuan walkers fielded by the [[Lords of Gardinaal]].  After being interred within a [[Contemptor Dreadnought]], however, Morn continued his service to Manus and would fight beside his [[Primarch]] during the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Dropsite Massacre]].  On that terrible day, Morn's service to his Primarch came to an end, when he was destroyed defending Manus' decapitated body on the blood-soaked ground of [[Isstvan V]].{{Fn|1}}

