Harjeon.wikitext:
{{TanithPortal}}
'''Harjeon''' was a [[Guardsman]] of the [[Tanith First and Only]] [[Imperial Guard Regiment|regiment]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|2}}


==Biography==
Harjeon was one of the [[Verghast]]ite recruits drafted into the regiment in the aftermath of the [[Siege of Vervunhive]]. Unlike a number of the other Verghastite Guardsmen who signed on, Harjeon had no formal combat experience prior to enlisting, which resulted in him being placed near the bottom of the informal "pecking order" that the new recruits fell into.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|2}} Despite this, he was considered one of the best of the new blood by [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]], the regiment's commanding officer.{{Fn|1b}}

Following the Siege of Vervunhive, the Tanith First was deployed on [[Hagia]]. During the retaking of the [[Holy Doctrinopolis]], [[Colonel]] [[Colm Corbec|Corbec]] was captured by the [[Infardi]]. Harjeon volunteered to accompany [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]] [[Gol Kolea|Kolea]] on a rescue mission despite the Tanith being ordered to evacuate the city in preparation for an impending armoured assault on the Doctrinopolis by the [[Eighth Pardus Armoured]].{{Fn|1a}}

Later, Harjeon joined the rest of his regiment in the [[Phantine (Planet)|Phantine]] theatre. Following the assault on the city of [[Cirenholm]], a combination of battlefield casualties and the pressing need to more fully integrate the Verghastite elements of the Tanith First led Colonel-Commissar Gaunt and [[Commissar]] [[Viktor Hark|Hark]] to put forward a number of Verghastite Troopers for consideration for promotion. Harjeon was suggested for one of the positions by Hark, but Gaunt rejected the decision, citing Harjeon's relative lack of respect from the other men in the regiment.{{Fn|2}}

