Haryk Thunderfang.wikitext:
{{DeathwatchPortal}}
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}'''{{Fn|2}} is a member of the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]] who was part of the [[Wolf Lord]] [[Ragnar Blackmane]]'s [[Great Company]] before he joined the [[Deathwatch]] as part of a [[Talasa Prime]] [[Kill-Team]] led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Artemis]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
In his service to the Deathwatch, Haryk took part in a mission that destroyed a [[Necron]] complex on the [[Necron Tomb World|Tomb World]] [[Norantis XIX]], which prevented the rest of the slumbering [[Xenos]] from awakening.{{Fn|2}}

Sometime later, Haryk's Kill-Team were called to meet with the [[Ordo Xenos]] [[Lord Inquisitor]] [[Kryptman]] and tasked with capturing alive several [[Genestealers]] from a [[Space Hulk]] that just emerged from the [[Warp]]. The Lord Inquisitor then planned to use the Genestealers to drive [[Hive Fleet Leviathan]] into the [[Ork Empire of Octarius]], thereby saving the [[Imperium]] worlds of [[Ultima Segmentum]] from the Devourer's grasp. After Captain Artemis gave his word to carry out Kryptman's mission, Haryk was forced to do so as well, though he did not think he would survive it.{{Fn|1a}}

However, Haryk did survive the successful mission and something later was released back to the Space Wolves. Afterwards, when the [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]] began, Haryk joined the [[Blackmanes]] Great Company in defending [[Cadia]], when the [[Fortress World]] was invaded by the forces of [[Chaos]].{{Fn|1b}}

