Hasfael.wikitext:
{{DarkAngelsPortal}}
'''Hasfael''' was a [[Librarian]] of the [[Dark Angels]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] active during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
In the Horus Heresy, Hasfael was part of the task force that [[Lion El'Jonson]] mustered when he learned that a secret [[Mechanicum]] facility in the [[Perditus System]] was under threat. He was aboard the ''[[Invincible Reason]]'' when it was trapped in a [[warp rift]] by the [[Night Lords]] vessel ''[[Avenging Shadow]]''. While there, [[Asmodeus]] called on his own [[psychic]] powers to protect the ''Invincible Reason'''s bridge from the [[Daemon|warp-creatures]] that had materialised aboard the ship. [[Brother-Redemptor]] [[Nemiel]] called for Asmodeus's execution as punishment for breaking the [[Edict of Nikaea]]. However, on learning from [[Seneschal]] [[Corswain]] and [[Chief Navigator]] [[Theralyn Fiana|Fiana]] that psychic attacks seemed to be the only effective weapons against the warp creatures, Lion El'Jonson overruled Nemiel and called on the three former librarians on board (Asmodeus, Hasfael and [[Alberein]]) to keep using their abilities to fight back. Nemiel protested at this, and the Lion killed him in response.{{Fn|1}}

