Hasturias Calaxor.wikitext:
{{AdeptusCustodesPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Venerable Contemptor Dreadnought]] within the [[Adeptus Custodes]] and has served for many millennia. 

==Biography==
[[Image:Hasturias Calaxor.jpg|thumb|right|{{PAGENAME}} when he was a Shield-Captain]]
He first came to prominence during the [[Horus Heresy]], when he [[Battle of Terra|defended]] the [[Imperial Palace]] from the [[Warmaster]]'s forces. During that massive battle, Calaxor single-handedly held the '''Enlightener's Star''' against the [[Traitor Guard]] of the [[9th Terran Wardens]]. He later rallied the [[Gospodor Heavy Infantry]] with his bravery and led them to retake the '''Dome of the Architects''' from [[Dortha Kol]]'s [[Sons of Horus]] Legionaries. While fighting beside other Custodes, Calaxor finally drove Kol's Legionaries to destruction, and felled the [[Traitor Titan Legion|traitor]] [[Warhound Titan]] ''[[Warp Jackal]]'' in the process as well. All these heroic accomplishments earned Calaxor the rank of [[Shield Captain]], even while the battle against the traitors raged on. After attaining his rank, Calaxor led three further highly successful counter-offensives before the siege’s end.{{Fn|1}}

Renowned for the controlled aggression of his tactics, Calaxor earned himself many more names in the centuries that followed. These included the defeat of the [[Daemon]] [[Thogralathrax]] on [[Thade (Planet)|Thade]], which prevented the [[Suppurant Scourge]] from being loosed on Terra, and the battle for the [[Star Fort|Star Keep]] ''[[Magnificence]]'', where he personally killed the heretical [[Singer of Miseries]] before leading a band of [[Vertus Praetor]]s to end the traitor threat on the Star Fort. It was Calaxor, also, whose blade eliminated the threat of the rogue [[Imperial Assassin]] [[Shae]] before she could come within a hundred miles of the [[Golden Throne]].{{Fn|1}}

When the Shield-Captain finally fell in battle on the [[Dead World]] [[Palathrix]], his sheer force of will kept him alive long enough to be interred within a [[Contemptor Dreadnought]] and allowed him to continue to serve [[Emperor of Mankind|the Emperor]]. Now a Venerable Ancient, he has assumed a new role within the Ten Thousand and serves the Custodes as both a living war engine and a strategic advisor for their forces.{{Fn|1}}

