Haxan the Defiler.wikitext:
{{RedCorsairsPortal}}
{{CrimsonFistsPortal}}
'''Haxan the Defiler''' was a former [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Crimson Fists]] [[Chapter]] and then leader of a [[Red Corsairs]] warband.{{Fn|1}}

==Overview==
'''''Haxan the Defiler''''' was known under the name of Captain '''Isidor Montes''' while serving in the [[Crimson Fists]].
As a Crimson Fist Captain, he led half a company of their warriors to suppress a alleged uprising on [[Hydra Secundus]]. What occurred there is unclear with the [[Inquisition]] claiming that Montes turned traitor and killed his own warriors and Montes himself claiming that the Inquisitor [[Matthias Rabe]] had declared [[exterminatus]] on an innocent planet to hide his own crimes. Montes claimed that witnessing this crime is what caused him to turn away from the Imperium after killing Rabe.{{Fn|1}}

Haxan the Defiler as he was known after this event, used the infamy of the event to become a member of the [[Red Corsairs]] and begun fighting the Imperium. Within twenty years, he had earned a warship and were striking at shrines across the [[Serpentis Reach]]. By 921.M41 he was the leader of a warband with a small fleet, using the Serpentis Reach as a base to raid deep into the [[Loki Sector]].{{Fn|1}}

Haxan the Defiler met his end as Matthias Rabe's pupil, Inquisitor [[Anatol Volk]] set up a trap using the [[Grand Cruiser]] [[Duchess Hespara]] as bait and using a squad of Crimson Fists, led by Sergeant [[Sandor Galleas]] to try and capture the heretic. Galleas refused to let the former Captain be taken by the Inquisition and instead executed him on the bridge of Duchess Hespara.{{Fn|1}}

==Source==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[None More Loyal (Short Story)]]


