Hectus Carmine.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Hectus Carmine''' was the [[Governor]] of the [[Talledus System]] in [[M36]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
When the mad [[Ecclesiarch]] [[Goge Vandire]] [[Reign of Blood|rose to power]], Carmine was one of the first to openly speak out against the [[High Lord of Terra]]. Vandire chose to make an example of Carmine and his people, invading [[Talledus]] itself with a vast army. After months of brutal fighting, Carmine and his "co-conspirators" were captured and trialled. Following a month of public torture, Carmine was burned alive on the steps of his own palace. Not content with this, Vandire ordered a series of purges across the [[Veritus Sub-Sector]].{{Fn|1}}

Eventually, [[Sebastian Thor]] rose up and overthrew Vandire. As part of his acts as the new Ecclesiarch, Thor visited a number of holy sites in the Veritus Sub-Sector. On visiting the ruins of Talledus, Thor ordered the construction of a grand monument to Carmine and decreed that, to honour those who fell defending Talledus (Carmine among them), the world would be renamed '''Benediction'''.{{Fn|1}}

