Helig Gallor.wikitext:
{{DeathGuardPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a warrior of the [[Death Guard]]'s 7th Great Company at the outbreak of the [[Horus Heresy]].

He was one of [[the Seventy]] who reached [[Terra]] aboard the frigate ''[[Eisenstein]]'' and were imprisoned in the [[Somnus Citadel]]. Some time later he volunteered to assist [[Amendera Kendel]] on a mission to [[Proxima Majoris]] for [[Malcador the Sigillite]].{{Fn|1}} Afterwards he became one of the [[Knights-Errant]] and was reunited with his [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]], [[Nathaniel Garro]], on [[Nolec Trimus]] where they defeated a dragon-like [[daemon]] together.{{fn|2}}

Later on [[Terra]], Gallor and his fellow Knights-Errant fought against [[Chaos Cultist]]s and the reborn [[Lord of the Flies]]. Along with Garro he was not among those chosen by Malcador to become a founding member of the [[Grey Knights]]. Instead, the two expressed their desire to fight [[Horus]] when he arrived at the Throneworld. Garro asked Gallor to gather as many of the surviving Seventy as he could.{{Fn|3}} During the [[Siege of Terra]] Gallor was one of the seven commanders selected by [[Rogal Dorn]] to lead a 100 men kill-squad to ambush the Sons of Horus beneath the [[Saturnine Gate]]. During the fighting, Gallor's squad met up with [[Garviel Loken]]'s squad and confronted the traitors led by [[Tormageddon]] together, leading to the demonhost's death.{{Fn|4}}

Continuing to fight alongside Garro during the Siege, Gallor was able to help [[Euphrati Keeler]] escape at Marmax Bastion while Garro sacrificed himself to hold off Mortarion himself.{{Fn|5}} He was later seen fighting alone in the final defense of the Inner Palace.{{Fn|6}}

