Helio Isidorus.wikitext:
{{ThousandSonsPortal}}
'''Helio Isidorus''' was a [[Legionary]] in the [[Thousand Sons]] [[Legion]], who fought the [[Space Wolves]] during the [[Burning of Prospero]]. As the Thousand Sons were beaten back by the Wolves, Helio and the other survivors of his shattered Legion were transported by [[Ahriman]] to the [[Planet of Sorcerers]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
On their new homeworld, Ahriman cast the [[Rubric of Ahriman]] in order to stop the mutations afflicting his brothers, which transformed Helio, and the other non-[[psychic]] members of the Thousand Sons, into [[Rubric Marine]]s. After his transformation Helio still retained some self awareness and occasionally recalled some memory of his past life, but these moments were always fleeting as his new form made it difficult for him to retain his thoughts.{{Fn|1}}

Helio later appeared at the side of the sorcerer [[Tolbek]], when he confronted Ahriman, traveling incognito with the Chaos warband [[The Harrowing]], aboard the ship ''[[Titan Child]]''.{{fn|2}}

After Ahriman's encounter with Amon and his Acquisition of the [[Athenaeum of Kallimakus]], Helio becomes one of the main subjects of Ahriman's research into the effects of the first Rubric and the creation of the second. Later, after Ahriman's supposed second Failure on the [[Planet of Sorcerers]], it is discovered that the second Rubric cast by Ahriman has partially worked, fully restoring Helio Isidorus as a Legionary, but at the price of most of his memories, seemingly only remembering his name.{{fn|3}}

In truth, after the casting of the second Rubric Helio's soul had become the vessel for a condition even worse, the [[Pyrodomon]]. He declared his intent to "unify" all of the Thousand Sons with the Pyrodomon, creating one eternal and unchanging entity.{{Fn|4a}} Despite the attempts of [[Ctesias]] and [[Ignis]] to contain Helio, he was able to infect large fleets of the Thousand Sons with the Pyrdomon, converting Sorcerers into Rubricae and causing existing Rubric Marines to combust.{{Fn|5a}} Ahriman was eventually able to use the [[Key of Infinity]] to travel into the past, destroying Helio's soul during the casting of the second rubric. In the new timeline created by Ahriman, Helio's armour is found aboard the ''[[Hekaton (Warship)|Hekaton]]'' to be empty and nameless.{{Fn|5b}}

