Hellas Sycar.wikitext:
{{SonsOfHorusPortal}}
[[Image:SycarValdor.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Hellas Sycar battles [[Constantin Valdor]] aboard the ''[[Vengeful Spirit]]'' in the climax of the [[Siege of Terra]]{{Fn|3a}}]]
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Sons of Horus]] active during the [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1}}

Replacing [[Falkus Kibre]] as commander of the [[Justaerin]] after Kibre's apparent death, by the final stages of the Siege Sycar was one of the more rational Sons of Horus commanders and was still sceptical of the powers of [[Chaos]]. Thus when [[Abaddon]] gathered the remaining Sons of Horus to make for the ''[[Vengeful Spirit]]'' after its [[Void Shield]]s were lowered, Sycar deferred to the First Captain's authority, unlike many.{{Fn|1}}

After arriving on the ''Vengeful Spirit'' alongside Abaddon, Sycar explored the reality-warped interior of the vessel alongside the First Captain. Eventually discovering the broken [[Kinor Argonis]],{{Fn|2a}} Sycar and his compatriots eventually became embattled against maddened [[Word Bearer]] legionaries and [[Solar Auxilia]]. Though they performed well, it took the intervention of [[Erebus]] to stop them being overwhelmed.{{Fn|2b}} Led by Abaddon, Sycar took part in a Justaerin assault on the [[Custodes]] aboard the ''Vengeful Spirit'' under [[Constantin Valdor]]. Aided by the powers of the [[Warp]] via Erebus and six other Justaerin Terminators, Sycar was able to badly wound Valdor with his sword.{{Fn|3a}}

Sycar later accompanied Abaddon and other surviving Sons of Horus officers when they finally reached [[Lupercal's Court]] and found [[Garviel Loken]] alongside the body of [[Horus]]. Sycar moved to attack Loken but was ordered to stand down by Abaddon, and later left the [[Sol System]] aboard the ''Vengeful Spirit''.{{Fn|3b}}

