Heptus Rho-Decima Khleng.wikitext:
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
'''Heptus Rho-Decima Khleng''' is the current [[Fabricator General]] of [[Metalica]] and he commanded both its and their allies' forces, during the [[Charadon Campaign]].{{Fn|1a}} 

==History==
Once a [[Cybernetica Datasmith|Datasmith]] of Metalica's [[Legio Cybernetica]], Khleng always revered the holy-machines he oversaw in battle. He was pivotal to Metalican victories on [[Scarvyn]], the [[Lanterior Purge]], and the quisition of [[Akhar Brosk]]'s lost datahives. Rising through the ranks and increasingly augmenting himself cybernetically, by the time he became Fabricator-General of Metalica his form was the size of a super-heavy tank. Moving upon a gravitic thrust cushion, he is festooned with nests of [[Mechadendrites]] and wreathes petrochemicals. His enormous body also contains a network of powerful [[Cogitator]]s whose innermost functions skirt the precipice of [[Abominable Intelligence]]. This gives him vast calculation and probability capabilities, which Khleng sees as the divine word of the [[Omnissiah]] himself.{{{Fn|1b}}

Since his ascension, Khleng has spent much time communing with the vast [[Noosphere]] data-network of his Forge World. Through this connection he can observe his entire domain and monitor all communications and data. If the Fabricator-General has one weakness, it is he stubbornly denies any possibility that violates his own predictions.{{Fn|1b}}

As the [[Charadon Campaign|Campaign]] raged, Khleng dispatched his [[Forge World]]'s forces to save the [[Invasion of Alumax|invaded]] [[Alumax System]], due to how close it was to [[Metalica]]. However the [[Chaos Lord|Plague Captain]] [[Oghlosmus Bilge]]'s [[Chaos Warband|warhost]], was too powerful for the [[System]]'s [[Imperial]] defenders and Alumax was conquered.{{Fn|2}} After a period of inactivity caused by shock, Khleng redoubled his efforts to reinforce Metalica and its outlying systems, withdrawing forces from the rest of the Sector in an abandonment known as Khleng's Betrayal. Trapped in a logic-loop of his own creation, he attempted to rationalize variables he viewed as factual impossibility and obsessed over minutia.{{Fn|1c}}

At the climax of the war in Charadon [[Typhus]] managed to breach Khleng's inner sanctum and infect him with the [[Nemesis Wurm]]. The computer phage spread throughout the Forge World and transformed Khleng into a mutated monstrosity. He was put out of his misery by Mechanicum repair teams.{{Fn|3}}

==Sources==
*1: [[War Zone Charadon - Act I: The Book of Rust]],
**{{Endn|1a}}: pg. 10
**{{Endn|1b}}: pg. 18
**{{Endn|1c}}: pg. 31
*{{Endn|2}}: [[White Dwarf 461]], pgs. 66-67 - Flashpoint: Alumax System
*{{Endn|3}}: [[War Zone Charadon - Act II: The Book of Fire]], pgs. 36-37
