Heqiroth.wikitext:
{{NecronsPortal}}
'''Heqiroth''' (also known as the '''Heqiroth of Nephrekh''') was a [[Necron]] vizier and dynastic advisor of the Overlord [[Turakhin]], later becoming an Overlord himself.{{Fn|1}}

== Overview ==
Heqiroth was one of the scions of the [[Nephrekh Dynasty]] before being brought under the wings of the [[Magadha Dynasty]] for the protection against alien invaders. These battles were fought by [[Khetmes]] who defended the borders of the [[Bor Enclave]]. Later he became involved in Khetmes's attempt to overthrow the Overlord via a single combat, leading to a failed coupe attempt. Using his involvement in a previous coup, he joined a conspiracy with [[Uluszekh]] and his co-conspirators, betraying it from within and thus, saving his overlord. At the peak of the victory he handed [[tesseract labyrinth]] to the overlord, successfully capturing him inside of it and thus, becoming a claimant to the throne.

As the claim was about to be confirmed by [[Metzoi]], [[Amontar]] stabbed Heqiroth with a poisoned dagger. Still, with the request repeated, Metzoi granted claimant the confirmation, thus: making him the new overlord of the Bor Enclave. While still wounded with the poisoned blade, the newly crowned overlord addressed the people of the Enclave via the [[holosphere]] and voiced his first command:
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"Judicator Metzoi, prepare the [[World Engine]].'''''{{Fn|1}}
|}}

== Personality ==
He wasn't a warrior, nor a cunning leader. But he was was praised by his overlord for his loyalty.

== Sources ==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The Lords of Borsis (Short Story)]]

