Herrik.wikitext:
{{ImperialKnightsPortal}}
'''Lady Herrik''' is a [[Freeblade Knight]], who aided in defending [[Abundantia]] during the [[Octarius War]], in [[M42]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
The [[Agri World]] was part of the [[Sigma-Ulstari System]], which had been repeatedly invaded by [[Orks]] and the [[Tyranids]] of [[Hive Fleet Leviathan]]. The [[Waaagh! Morbad|Waaagh!]] of [[Speedboss]] [[Morbad Zagblasta]] was among the latest to do so and he led his hordes to invade [[Abundantia]]. During his attack, Lady Herrik defended '''Refinery Torqad-Upsilon''', alongside the maniples of [[Sigma-Ulstari (Forge World)|Sigma-Ulstari]]'s [[Skitarii]] and the [[3,981st Vorrdi Light Sappers]] [[Regiment]]. They were also able to prepare a significant defense, once they learned the Orks were looting the Refinery's outlying sub-stations. However when the attack finally came, it was an airborne armada that was led by the infamous [[Flyboy]] [[Manik Gorg]]. While many of the Orks' aircraft were shot down, there was simply too many for the defenders to overcome. Manik was among the Orks that swarmed the defenders and the Flyboy's style of warfare was to unload his weapons, before crashing into his foes with his [[Deffkopta]]. As the Orks swarmed the Imperial defenders, Manik targeted Lady Herrik to slam into, but only managed a glancing blow to one of the [[Freeblade Knight]]'s knees. This was enough to unbalance her, though, and she also began to be attacked by other Ork aircraft. Because of this, Herrik was left unable to turn and attack the Flyboy, as Manik once again charged at her. This time, the Flyboy's Deffkopta fully connected with the Freeblade Knight and caused her to topple to the ground. Ork [[Blitza-Bommer]]s then destroyed a huge skeletal gantry in the refinery, which collapsed on top of Lady Herrik. While she survived its impact, the fuming Freeblade Knight was left trapped beneath the gantry's wreckage.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[White Dwarf 470]], pg. 24 - ''The Red and The Dead Part 1'' 

