Hexachires.wikitext:
{{DarkEldarPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}} Ulthiliad'''{{Fn|1e}} is a [[Dark Eldar]] [[Haemonculus]] of the [[Coven of the Thirteen Scars]]. Known as the '''Lord of the Synod of Scars''', he is the highest-ranked Haemonculi in the Coven.{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
A truly ancient individual, during the days of the [[Eldar Empire]] Hexachires was an unsuccessful artist. After the [[Fall of the Eldar]] he managed to flee to the safety of [[Commorragh]], where he rose to become a powerful Haemonculus within the Thirteen Scars with the help of the [[Harlequin]] [[Shadowseer]] [[Sylandri Veilwalker]].{{Fn|1e}} He later became one of [[Fabius Bile]]'s tutors during his time in [[Commorragh]] but swore revenge against the [[Chaos Space Marine Apothecary|Chief Apothecary]] after he fled the Dark City and instigated a destructive war as cover. Hexachires subsequently allied with [[Archon]] [[Peshig]] of the [[Kabal of the Bloody Blossom]] and Archon [[Salar]] of the [[Kabal of the Hanging Skull]] to seek out Bile.{{Fn|1a}}

During the [[Battle of Belial IV]] Hexachires attempted to crush Bile once and for all, but was foiled due by the Chief Apothecary and the betrayal of his allies. He subsequently was forced to escape once [[Daemon]]s arrived.{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}

Hexachires is secretly a follower of [[Ynnead]] and sees awakening the god as the only way to save the Eldar race from its doom. He believes that by instigating the Drukhari to destroy one another, Ynnead's power will be fueled. However Hexachires does not plan to perish with the rest of his kin and sees himself as a shepherd for the galaxy's life after Ynnead awakens.{{Fn|1d}}

