Heymlik Chass.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Heymlik Chass'''{{Fn|Note 1}} was the Patriarch of the [[Noble House]] [[House Chass|Chass]] at the time of the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
Although House Chass was one of the oldest and most powerful of [[Vervunhive]]'s noble houses, Lord Heymlik Chass himself was regarded by his peers as weak due to his more liberal views and perceived lack of guile. He was also in a precarious position as, unlike the Lords of other powerful Houses like [[House Anko|Anko]] and [[House Croe|Croe]], Heymlik was openly critical of the leadership of [[Salvador Sondar]] (Lord of [[House Sondar]] and High Master of Vervunhive). As a result, Heymlik's daughter and only heir, [[Merity Chass|Merity]], was extremely protective of him.{{Fn|1c}}

When Vervunhive was [[Siege of Vervunhive|attacked]] by the [[Chaos|Fallen]] [[Ferrozoica|Hive Ferrozoica]] in the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]], Heymlik disagreed with most of the other Houses' representatives and [[General]] [[Noches Sturm]] (commander of the [[Astra Militarum|Imperial Guard]] taskforce sent by [[Warmaster]] [[Macaroth]] to aid the efforts on [[Verghast]]) as to the best plan of defence for the hive. Heymlik was not the only dissenter, however, as [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]] and [[Coron Grizmund|a number]] [[Nash|of other Guard]] officers protested Sturm's plan.{{Fn|1b}} This led Heymlik to invite Gaunt to his residence; having studied Gaunt's career and determining him to be an honourable man and a decisive and effective military commander, he sought to ally with Gaunt, anticipating that the Siege would go badly under the likes of Sondar, Sturm, [[Edric Croe|Croe]] and [[Heskith Anko|Anko]]. On meeting Gaunt, both Lord Chass and his daughter agreed that Gaunt would indeed be an ally for them; Heymlik presented Gaunt with a metal rose as a sign of his support.{{Fn|1c}}

Later in the battle for Vervunhive, Heymlik's worst fears were realised when Salvador Sondar, corrupted by the whispers of Chaos, dropped the [[Void Shield|energy field]] protecting the hive.{{Fn|1d}} After ordering [[Rudrec|his chief bodyguard]] to escort Merity to a shelter{{Fn|1d}}, Heymlik led a team of his bodyguards to stop Sondar but was fatally wounded while fighting Sondar's tainted [[servitor]]s.{{Fn|1e}} As he bled out, more Imperials arrived to stop Sondar, one team sent by Marshal Croe under the command of [[Isak]] and a group of [[Imperial Guardsmen]] including Gaunt.{{Fn|1e}}

Although Heymlik did not survive, the remaining Imperials destroyed the servitors, killed Salvador Sondar and turned the shield back on.{{Fn|1e}} Heymlik would posthumously return the favour to Gaunt in the final stages of the war; the metal rose that Gaunt had been wearing protected him when he was shot in the heart by the Chaos warlord [[Heritor Asphodel]] and saved his life.{{Fn|1f}}


