Hierax.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion's]] [[22nd Chapter (Ultramarines Legion)|22nd Chapter]] and commanded its [[Destroyer Marine|Second Destroyer Company]] during the [[Great Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
Born on [[Terra]], Hierax was his Chapter's most senior Captain when [[Lord Commander (Legiones Astartes)|Chapter Master]] [[Machon Phalaris|Phalaris]] was killed in battle against the [[ork]]s of the [[Thoas|Thoas Empire]].{{Fn|1a}} As a result, it was expected that Hierax would take command of the 22nd, according to the Chapter's traditions. To his Chapter's shock, however, the Legion's [[Primarch]], [[Roboute Guilliman]], bypassed Hierax and instead promoted{{Fn|1b}} Captain [[Eleon Iasus]] of the [[166th Company (Ultramarines Legion)|166th Company]] to command.{{Fn|1a}} This was done deliberately, as the Primarch hoped that by giving an outsider command of the 22nd, Iasus would bring Hierax's non-standard Chapter into line with the wider culture of the Ultramarines Legion.{{Fn|1b}}

This decision did not sit well with Hierax or his Chapter{{Fn|1b}}, but over the following battles of the Great Crusade and [[Horus Heresy]], it was proven that Guilliman had made the right choice. Under Iasus' influence and decisions, the 22nd Chapter was reshaped into a weapon the Primarch was not ashamed to unleash in battle and the trust between Hierax and Iasus ran deep. They both valued each other's skills and in the matters of strategy, Iasus always consulted Hierax for his judgement, with the Captain having absolute faith that any decision Iasus then made was the correct one.{{Fn|2}}

As the Horus Heresy neared its end, Hierax was among his Legion's forces that Guilliman led to [[Terra]], in the hope that they would reach the world before it was [[Battle for Terra|invaded]] by the [[Warmaster]]'s forces. However, the Ultramarines had to pass through the [[Carchera System]] to do so and were forced to fight the [[Iron Warriors]] of [[Warsmith]] [[Khrossus]] who had seized control of the System.{{Fn|2}}

