Hierek Mon.wikitext:
{{SonsOfHorusPortal}}
'''Hierek Mon''' was a [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] in the [[Sons of Horus]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]] and was a member of its [[Warrior Lodges]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was well known within the Sons of Horus for his skill in void warfare and had an enviable kill-tally in the later years of the Great Crusade. When the [[Horus Heresy]] began, Mon joined his Legion in turning upon the [[Imperium]] and by then had command of the [[Hunter Destroyer|Destroyer]] ''[[Grey Talon]]''. The ''Talon'' had a reputation that promised advancement for its crew, but its prestige ended due to Mon's actions during the [[Battle of Isstvan III]]. As the purging of the [[Traitor Legion]]'s Loyalists occurred, Mon had been ordered to remain as part of the high-orbit blockade above [[Isstvan III]], but he joined the warships bombarding the world after the [[Primarch]] [[Angron]] personally took part in the battle. For his defiance, Mon was placed in a suicidal position during the Traitors' fleet deployment in the [[Dropsite Massacre]]. Though Mon was expected to atone for his failures by dying in the battle, his skill kept the ''Grey Talon'' alive, as the fleets of the Loyalist Legions were shattered. However his luck finally ran out, after his ship was boarded by [[Salamanders]], led by Captain [[Xa'ven]], who used a Traitor Dropship Lander they had captured on [[Isstvan V]] to get past the ''Talon's'' guard. In the boarding attack that followed, Mon and the forces under his command were killed and the ''Grey Talon'' was taken by the Loyalists, who used it to escape from the Traitor Legions.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Grey Talon (Short Story)]]

