Hildegarde Matliss.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Hildegarde Matliss''' was a [[Cadian]] [[General]], who served{{Fn|1a}} in the [[Indomitus Crusade]]'s [[Battle Group Tartaros]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
Though she was considered an aging relic of [[Cadian]] glory, Matliss had more victories under her belt than the rest of [[Battle Group Tartaros|Tartaros]]' officers combined. Also after years of campaigning with the [[Battle Group]]'s forces, the [[General]] had become the lynchpin for the various political strands that held Tartaros together. Because of this, Matliss was considered to be its talisman and was greatly respected by the Battle Group's members. Her years of service later ended on [[Attruso]], however,{{Fn|1a}} as Tartaros attempted to reclaim the rebellious [[Carrodan System]] from the [[T'au Empire]].{{Fn|1b}} It was as she commanded the Battle Group's [[Astra Militarum]] forces on the besieged world, that she was slain by a [[Sniper]] while disembarking from a shuttle. The shot came from a considerable distance away and two of Matliss' [[Imperial Guard Command Squad|Command Squad]] were killed by the sniper as well, shortly after she was struck. The General's death was a blow to the Battle Group's forces and everyone also knew, that her absence would also have long reaching consequences for Tartaros as a whole. The war for Attruso raged on though, and [[Colonel]] [[Wassenby]] was chosen to succeed Matliss as the Militarum's commander in the invasion.{{Fn|1a}}

