Holzhauer.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
{{Spoiler|source= Traitor Rock (Novel)}}
'''Holzhauer''' was a [[Elnaur Chasseurs]] [[Marshal|Lord-Marshal]], who turned upon the [[Imperium]] and declared himself the '''Arch-Duke''' of the [[Malouri Uprising]].{{Fn|1b}} 
==History==
This occurred on [[Malouri]] after news of [[Cadia]]'s destruction, during the [[13th Black Crusade]], began to spread despite the [[Imperium]]'s efforts to stop it. [[Eris Bellona]], who was a [[Priest]] to one Holzhauer's [[Elnaur Chasseurs]] [[Regiment]]s, learned of this and became despondent. He believed the Imperium was now close to being destroyed, but he later wrote{{Fn|1a}} a thesis on how to save it. The key factor of this, was to return the Imperium to the age when [[Goge Vandire]] ruled over [[Mankind]]. For this to happen, though, a cleansing purge would have to take place. Though a fellow [[Ecclesiarchy]] Adept declared them to be [[Heresy]], the words did not seem so to Holzhauer. Instead they expressed truths that he had never seen written before. Holzhauer was particularly drawn to the thesis' call for a military leader for the purging [[Crusade]], that would save the Imperium. The Lord-Marshal's arrogance and ambition made him believe he was that leader. In Holzhauer's mind, divine providence had brought this opportunity to him and he had to act. He informed Bellona that he would lead the Crusade{{Fn|1b}} and the Lord Marshal soon gathered others to Bellona's cause. And this began the [[Malouri Uprising]].{{Fn|1c}}

