Honorius Luciel.wikitext:
{{ambig|subject=Ultramarine|disambiguation=Honorius}}
{{ambig|subject=Ultramarine|disambiguation=Luciel}}
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Honorius Luciel''' was an officer of the [[Ultramarines]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] active at the tail end of the [[Great Crusade]]. By that point he served as the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the Legion's [[209th Company (Ultramarines Legion)|209th Company]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
At one point in the Great Crusade, Luciel led his company during [[Caskian Campaign|a campaign]] on [[Caskian]] against an insectoid [[xenos]] species. While deployed on Caskian, Luciel and the 209th fought alongside a [[Space Marine Company|company]] of the [[Word Bearers]] Legion led by [[Sorot Tchure]]. Despite the tense relationship between their Legions (a result of [[Emperor of Mankind|the Emperor]] having had the Ultramarines destroy the city of [[Monarchia]] to censure the Word Bearers' defiance of the [[Imperial Truth]]), Luciel struck up a friendship with Tchure.{{Fn|1c}}

Eight years later{{Fn|1c}}, when the Ultramarines and Word Bearers Legions mustered above the planet [[Calth]] prior to [[Ghaslakh Crusade|a planned action]] against the [[ork]]s of the [[Ghaslakh xenohold]]{{Fn|1b}}, Luciel and his company were assigned to guard [[Numinus High Anchor]], a fleet anchor station above [[Numinus City]]. Luciel had personally requested the assignment, as this would allow him to meet with his friend Tchure once again.{{Fn|1a}}

At one point during the muster, Luciel did indeed meet Tchure aboard the [[cruiser]] ''[[Samothrace]]''. When the Word Bearers [[Chaos|abruptly revealed their true allegiances]] at the start of the [[Horus Heresy]], Luciel and 17 Marines under his direct command were murdered by a group of Tchure's Word Bearers. Many commentaries on [[Battle of Calth|the battle that followed]] would credit Luciel and his men as the first Loyalist casualties, although others held that, strictly speaking, the crew of the fleet tender ''[[Campanile]]'' (who had earlier been slaughtered in a clandestine boarding action) died before Luciel.{{Fn|1a}}

==Wargear==
By the end of the Great Crusade, Luciel wore a suit of [[Space Marine Power Armour#Mark IV "Maximus Armour"|Praetor-pattern power armour]] manufactured on [[Veridia Forge]].{{Fn|1a}}

==Sources==
