Honyaegar.wikitext:
{{ImperialNavyPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[Imperial Navy Captain]] who commands the [[Apocalypse Class Battleship]] ''[[Triumph (ship)|Triumph]]'' and was brought into [[Battlefleet Armageddon]] in 951.[[M41]] following the aftermath of the [[Second War for Armageddon]]. He commanded what remained of the Battlefleet and the ''Triumph'' proved to be the bane of many pirate fleets keen to take advantage of any weakness in the devastated [[Armageddon Subsector]]. Under {{PAGENAME}}'s command the ''Triumph'' went on to amass an impressive roll of honour and became the symbol of the [[Emperor of Mankind|Emperor's]] will within the Sub-Sector. A generation later however, an increase in [[Ork]] attacks on [[System]]s surrounding [[Armageddon]] started to drastically cut the amount of merchant shipping voyaging to the main System and the Triumph and other ships in the Battlefleet, found themselves stretched to the breaking point. There were simply too few ships to cover so much space and it was the merchant transports that were feeling the effect. An appeal for reinforcements was met by the arrival of [[Admiral]] [[Parol]], on board ''[[His Will]]'', and three first line Cruiser squadrons. Acknowledging the Admiral's seniority and greater experience, Captain {{PAGENAME}}  transferred command of the Battlefleet to Parol and, for a short time, the depredations of the Ork pirates abated. This all changed, almost overnight, as the Ork piratical raids turned into full blown planetary assaults of several minor systems and the [[Third War for Armageddon]] began.{{Fn|1}}

As Admiral Parol led the Battlefleet into battle with the invading Orks, {{PAGENAME}} took part as well and fought in the [[Battle of Pelucidar]]. That battle nearly proved to be the Triumph's end, as Ork [[Kroozer]]s teleported a large number of Orks onto the Battleship, once its shields were brought down. Captain {{PAGENAME}} reluctantly gave the order to disengage from the battle, a feat he barely manged in his crippled vessel, though the fighting to clear the Ork boarders from the ''Triumph'' reportedly took another four days to complete.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[White Dwarf 279 (UK)]], pgs. 62–63 — ''Battlefleet Gothic: War on all Fronts''

