Hookey (Mordian Iron Guard).wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Hookey''' is a roguish [[Ratling]] in the [[Mordian 24th]] and is also one of the best [[Ratling Sniper|sniper]]s in the [[Mordian Iron Guard]] [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
The [[Mordian 24th]] is among the [[Mordian Iron Guard|Iron Guard]] that are taking part in the [[Third War for Armageddon]] and and were set to counter-attack against [[Ork]] forces on the '''Sulphur River'''.{{Fn|1a}} However Hookey feigned an illness to get out of the battle and was instead left behind with [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] [[Kaine (Captain)|Kaine]]'s [[Platoon|3rd Platoon]].{{Fn|1b}} It was charged with guarding the [[Regiment]]'s supplies, within a ruined mine that was close to the Sulphur River's '''Asch Creek''', until the 24th returned. Unfortunately disaster struck soon afterwards, when the Regiment was almost completely destroyed by an Ork ambush and its few survivors were unable to warn Kaine about their defeat. An Ork [[Warboss]] then led a horde against the unsuspecting Platoon{{Fn|1a}} and Hookey, along with the Hive Militia and civilians the 24th left behind as well.{{Fn|1b}} Though vastly outnumbered, the 3rd is unaware that the Orks only have a limited time to battle the Platoon, before the horde has to return to the Xenos' main camp.{{Fn|1a}}
==Trivia==
*The [[Mordian 24th]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Jervis Johnson]]. They were featured in [[Citadel Journal 48]].{{Fn|1a}}
*The ''Last Stand at Asch Creek'' is a modified version of the [[Battle of Glazer's River]] scenario, which appeared in [[White Dwarf 222 (UK)]]. Besides the change in [[Regiment]] and location,{{Fn|1a}} the [[Platoon]] is led by [[Kaine (Captain)|Kaine]], instead of [[Caine (Captain)|Caine]]. The names of the characters Hookey and Blikk, however, remain the same.{{Fn|1b}} 

