Horatio Bugler.wikitext:
{{ImperialNavyPortal}}
[[Fleet Admiral]] '''Horatio Bugler''' was a celebrated officer of the [[Imperial Navy]].{{Fn|1a}}

==History==
Early in his career, the young [[Imperial Navy Captain|Captain]] Bugler was assigned to command of the [[Falchion Escort]] ''[[Escapade]]'', on its maiden voyage from the shipyards at [[Voss Prime]].{{Fn|1a}}

Though Bugler, his crew, and the ''Falchion'' class as a whole were untested in combat, they had considerable success in their first engagement over [[Adumbria]] in 938.[[M41]].{{Fn|1}}  The ''Escapade'' and its sister ship the ''[[Virago]]'' were the only Imperial vessels on station when the [[Ravagers (Warband)|Ravagers]] armada of a dozen or more vessels emerged from the [[Warp]].  Though unable to stop the Chaos forces landing their troops, both vessels were able to slip into the null-fire zone to the aft of the Chaos ships, destroying two with [[torpedo]] volleys and a third with their [[weapons batteries]], before the Chaos forces returned fire.  Again, their superior speed and maneuverability allowed the ''Falchions'' to disengage without taking significant damage.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}}

Bugler would then go on to much greater fame and success.  [[Inquisitor]] [[Amberley Vail]] noted the irony that at least two celebrated Imperial officers appeared, during the early phases of their careers, with her subject, [[Commissar]] [[Ciaphas Cain]], though unlike the other, [[Jenit Sulla]], Bugler had (mercifully) not yet decided to publish his memoirs.{{Fn|1a}}

