Hy'Galas.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Hy'Galas''' was an [[Imperial]], whose scriptures led him to be declared an [[Heretic|Arch-Heretic]] and he was later executed by the [[Inquisition]] in 0.762.1324.[[M33]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
In his works, Hy'Galas described the [[Emperor]] as an unmoving carcass and not a [[Ecclesiarchy|divine being]] who controlled every aspect of the [[Imperium]]. Hy'Galas also stated that while the [[High Lords of Terra]] now ruled the Imperium and tried to interpret the Emperor's will, they had no hope of truly filling His role. For Hy'Galas thought the Emperor's empire was too vast and filled with groups who had conflicting interests. He stated these groups worked secretly within the Imperium to exert their influence over it and remarked that the the [[Navis Nobilite]] was among them. While many speculated about the the [[Navigator]]s' shrouded history, Hy'Galas claimed he found the truth of the matter, through ancient texts held by the [[Inquisition]]. Though he stated they were held in the Inquisition's most secured record-crypts, Hy'Galas was somehow able to gain access to these texts and the knowledge they held. After doing so, he wrote a detailed history of the Navis Nobilite from its early history, as the Emperor's creation to navigate the [[Warp]], all the way to the powerful group's inner workings circa [[M33]]. Hy'Galas also briefly described several [[Navigator House]]s, which included [[House M'edici|M'edici]], [[House Locarno|Locarno]], [[House Hals-Viati|Hals-Viati]], [[House Sixtus|Sixtus]], [[House Davor-Jarni|Davor-Jarni]], [[House Emed-Useli|Emed-Useli]] and the destroyed [[House D'Kark]].{{Fn|1}} 

However Hy'Galas' scriptures, later led him to be declared an [[Heretic|Arch-Heretic]] and he was executed by the [[Inquisition]], via flagellation, in 0.762.1324.[[M33]]. Despite his status as a Heretic, though, the Inquisition has kept Hy'Galas' scriptures for their records. Only they have clearance to read his works, but even then, it has been noted that several pages of Hy'Galas' scriptures have been permanently wiped away.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
*''Hy'Galas'' was created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Warwick Kinrade]] and he was featured in [[The Citadel Journal 18]].{{Fn|1}}
*His name is spelled in all capital letters, so it is not known if it is presented as ''Hy'Galas'' or ''Hy'galas''.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The Citadel Journal 18]], pgs. 26-30 - ''Navigators''

